# Language (project)

- Write **all** of the following in **English (US)** unless a file is explicitly a localized resource (e.g. `package.nls.ru.json`):
  - UI strings, command titles, notifications, and button labels in VS Code extension code and `package.json` `contributes.*` text.
  - User-facing `README`, `docs/` intended for contributors and end users, CLI help, and error messages shown in the editor.
  - Identifiers in examples and public API names (already English by convention).
- **Code comments**: English, short and purposeful.
- Prefer **American spelling** (e.g. "color", "initialize") in UI and docs.

If you add Russian localization later, keep English as the default/source strings; put Russian only in dedicated `nls`/locale files.
